# {{name}}

A juiz component written in Python. It was made with `juiz pkg create --idl` of juiz {{juiz_version}},
from the process / container declarations of `{{idl_main}}`.

License: {{license}}

## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `{{idl_main}}` | The types and the declarations (JIDL) |
| `app/python/{{name}}.py` | The Component. Each decorated function is a type. Write the bodies (`raise NotImplementedError`) |
| `app/python/<namespace>/` | The Python types (record, enum) of the `.jidl`, generated by `juiz idl -g python` (do not edit) |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz and Python versions) |
| `pyproject.toml` | The Python packages this project uses (pyjuiz) |
| `scripts/pack.sh`, `scripts/pack.ps1` | Make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |

## Requirements

- juiz {{juiz_version}} with Python support (`juiz --version`). `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}` in the venv below is the easiest
- Python 3.10 or later

`pyjuiz` in `pyproject.toml` is pinned to the same version as juiz (`=={{juiz_version}}`).
When you update juiz, update `pyjuiz` to the same version.

